        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "a candidate of dark matter, the primordial black holes (PBHs) may be originated by comoving curvature perturbations generated when inflation reenters the horizon [30]. By inspecting the accompanying GW radiation, Taiji has the potential to probe PBHs in the mass range of  $ 10^{-16} \\sim 10^{-10} M_{\\odot} $ [31, 32], offering a unique window to test PBH hypothesis.",
            "block_bbox": [
                100,
                107,
                1127,
                198
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 1,
            "block_polygon_points": [
