        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The TDC II datasets contain both isotropic SGWB and confusion galactic binaries (CGBs). The latter constitutes an anisotropic background due to the inhomogeneous distribution of binaries in the Milky Way, exhibiting a year-round modulation pattern. We postpone the issue of CGB to future work. At this stage, we pre-process the dataset by subtracting the provided CGB component and focus our analysis on the residual noise and isotropic background.",
